WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
The One Piece Manga just revealed that Princess&nbsp;
Vivi might rejoin with Luffy and the straw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.540
hats very soon. It turns out that she managed to&nbsp;
escape from the world government after her father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.700
the king of Alabasta, was assassinated during the&nbsp;
meeting of the world’s most powerful kingdoms. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:20.220
she is now inside the flying ship of Big News&nbsp;
Morgan, the mysterious man who controls the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.380
media of the one piece world, which is flying&nbsp;
over Egghead Island. Which leaves us with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.000
very important question: Who will actually&nbsp;
join the straw hats at the end of this arc?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.480
Because next to Dr. Vegapunk, there&nbsp;
are now suddenly 3 possible female&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.860
candidates for the next straw hat&nbsp;
member: Jewelry Bonney, Stussy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.000
now Vivi. And let’s be real, the crew could really&nbsp;
use a 3rd female member next to Nami and Robin. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.140
while Oda has disappointed his fans quite&nbsp;
a few times now, by teasing Rebecca,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.860
Carrot or Yamato joining the crew,&nbsp;
before ultimately nothing happening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:52.800
there is a lot of evidence, that this time things&nbsp;
might be different. So let’s look at each of our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.620
three candidates and why they might be the 10th&nbsp;
member Luffy has wanted for his pirate crew.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.600
Starting with Stussy. At first glance, Stussy&nbsp;
seems to be the most unlikely choice for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.760
becoming a straw hat. Up until a few chapters&nbsp;
ago, we thought that she was an enemy agent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.860
who wanted to capture or even kill Luffy&nbsp;
for the world government. Oda then stunned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.480
his entire fanbase by revealing that&nbsp;
Stussy was in reality a double agent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:24.360
who had been spying on the government for Dr.&nbsp;
Vegapunk all along. She betrayed Lucci and Kaku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.340
much like they betrayed their ship wright comrades&nbsp;
on Water 7 and she then started helping Vegapunk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.440
and the straw hats to escape the island. And the&nbsp;
biggest argument for why Stussy would not join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:39.660
Luffy is of course the fact, that she barely has&nbsp;
had any interaction with the straw hats so far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:45.180
She has no relationship to Luffy at all and we&nbsp;
don’t know if she has a dream that would align&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:50.880
with Luffy becoming pirate king. However,&nbsp;
you might be surprised how good of a straw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:56.460
hat candidate she actually is. As you probably&nbsp;
know, Stussy is actually the first successfully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.980
cloned human being in one piece history. She was&nbsp;
created by Vegapunk and his team of scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:07.260
as a replica of Miss Buckinham Stussy. Not only&nbsp;
was she a member of this crew of mad scientists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.360
but she also is the mother of Weevil and&nbsp;
a former member of the Rocks pirate crew.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:11.760
Now we don’t yet know much about clone Stussy’s&nbsp;
past. But it is clear that she must have had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:18.360
a tragic one. Dr Vegapunk tells us, that as a&nbsp;
clone, he always saw her as human, while most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.820
other people didn’t. So Stussy must have lived&nbsp;
a life where people around her didn’t even see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:31.020
her as a real person, but as a monster, similar to&nbsp;
Chopper. She was then ordered by Vegapunk to spend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:35.640
her entire life as a double agent. She had to go&nbsp;
through the terrible training of the governments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:42.060
secret agent program, kill countless people at&nbsp;
their orders and take on even more fake identities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:48.540
as a member of CP0. In other words, Stussy must&nbsp;
be a person with the worst identity crisis in all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:54.240
of One Piece. She doesn’t know if she is a real&nbsp;
person, nor did she have any real relationships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:59.580
her entire life. And even the one person she&nbsp;
is loyal to, Vegapunk, had no problem using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:05.280
her as a tool her entire life. So while Stussy&nbsp;
looks very cool and composed on the surface,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:11.460
I wouldn’t be at all surprised if we saw a&nbsp;
really dark and vulnerable side of her. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:17.640
would of course check one of the most important&nbsp;
boxes any new straw hat needs: A tragic past.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:23.280
And since Vegapunk is not the person who will give&nbsp;
Stussy the sense of belonging she probably needs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:31.500
Oda could be setting up a moment where Luffy can&nbsp;
save her from her darkness. After all, every last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:39.120
straw hat was saved by Luffy in some way or form.&nbsp;
Which is often both physically and mentally. Nami&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.400
from being a servant to Arlong and her loneliness&nbsp;
and pain for lying to her village. Brook from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:50.040
florian triangle and from being lonely after&nbsp;
losing his entire crew. Or Robin, from being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:55.440
captured by the world government and from being&nbsp;
lonely after a life of being hunted and betrayed.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:02.340
In fact, Stussy’s story might be quite similar to&nbsp;
Robin. Both of them worked for organizations they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.200
didn’t like. Both have made an enemy of the&nbsp;
world goverment. You could argue that Stussy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:13.920
right now is quite similar to Robin joining&nbsp;
the crew after Alabasta. No one saw it coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:19.800
and we didn’t know much about her until we got&nbsp;
to water 7, where we also have the parallel to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:26.940
Lucci and CP0. And Stussy has no other place to&nbsp;
go right now, but to sail with the Straw hats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:32.760
So Stussy could join the crew in a casual looking&nbsp;
way right now, until she gets her real arc later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:37.920
on in the story. Her role in the crew would of&nbsp;
course be that of a spy and I also think that in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:44.040
terms of power she would make a great addition to&nbsp;
the crew. She is a former Rocks member after all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:49.320
And similar to Robin, the straw hats could&nbsp;
become the first real family she ever had,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:55.560
with Luffy saving her from her own darkness,&nbsp;
acknowledging her as her own unique person.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:01.620
Which now brings me to our candidate Nr. 2:&nbsp;
Vivi. For Vivi, many fans have long speculated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:06.300
that she would reunite with the crew and&nbsp;
become a full-blown straw hat. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.980
some people will tell you that she has been&nbsp;
a member of Luffy’s crew all this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:15.360
similar to how Jinbei only joined up with the&nbsp;
rest of the crew during Wano. So really there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:21.300
are only 2 big arguments why Vivi wouldn’t join:&nbsp;
First, you could make a fairly strong argument,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:27.840
that Vivi’s arc is already over. Her dream was&nbsp;
to free her country from the rule of Crocodile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:34.080
which Luffy helped her achive. And second, unless&nbsp;
she had a secret Kobe-level training arc over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:39.840
time skip, there is simply no way that Vivi&nbsp;
would be even close to the power level of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:45.240
crew right now. So her joining the crew would&nbsp;
purely be based on her experience as a ruler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:51.240
and diplomat and on her previous relationship&nbsp;
with the crew. That being said though, I have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:56.940
always believed that there is a really good chance&nbsp;
that Vivi will in fact become the 10th member.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:02.040
Vivi was basically guaranteed to join the crew&nbsp;
until the final twist at the end of Alabasta,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:07.380
where she chose her country over her personal&nbsp;
dream to sail with Luffy. With the murder of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:12.480
her father however, things have changed. We&nbsp;
know that Imu, the secret ruler of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:17.460
seems to be targeting the Royal family of&nbsp;
Albasta. So it’s very likely that Vivi only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:21.120
survived the meeting of the Kings,&nbsp;
because she was able to escape with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:25.020
Morgans. So while she couldn’t join the crew&nbsp;
before, because of her duty to her country,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:30.000
she now has nowhere to go. Not only is&nbsp;
she really close to Luffy right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.000
but Luffy is also her best chance to save&nbsp;
her country from the governments anger. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.920
her dream is once again aligned with Luffy’s.&nbsp;
We already know that she vibes extremely well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:45.000
with everyone in the crew, she has been&nbsp;
to Marijois before and she would represent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.160
Alabasta joining sides with Joy Boy once again,&nbsp;
just how it happened during the void century.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:56.040
But despite the really strong cases we have&nbsp;
for both Vivi and Stussy joining the crew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.040 --> 00:08:02.520
the by far most likely candidate for the next&nbsp;
straw hat, is in fact our candidate nr 3:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:07.080
Bonney. As my dear friend mr morj explained&nbsp;
in one of his videos recently, there might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:12.780
not have been a better straw hat candidate than&nbsp;
Bonney in One Piece since Luffy invited Jinbei&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:18.480
back on Fishman Island. And even if she didn’t&nbsp;
join the crew officially, it seems pretty much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:23.460
guaranteed at this point that she will travel&nbsp;
with the Straw hats for at least the next arc&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:27.780
or two. There is really only one good reason why&nbsp;
she wouldn’t be able to join the crew right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:33.540
and that’s the fact that Bonney has her own&nbsp;
pirate ship and crew, because she is a member of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:39.360
the worst generation. However even that argument&nbsp;
doesn’t seem to quite hold up anymore. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:45.720
every time we have seen Bonney since the time&nbsp;
skip, there has been no trace of either her crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:50.640
or her ship. In fact, it seems very likely&nbsp;
that they might have been killed. One time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.260
Bonney gets captured by Blackbeard after the war&nbsp;
at marineford, so he might have defeated her crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:00.780
there. Or it might have happened right before she&nbsp;
was fished out of the water by the straw hats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:05.460
when they reached Egghead Island. That would&nbsp;
explain why she was drifting in the icy ocean.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:11.940
Bonney has been built up to be one of the most&nbsp;
important characters in the story for the endgame.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:17.700
Not only is she inspired by Anne Bonney, THE&nbsp;
most famous real female pirate in history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:24.270
but as Morj rightfully noticed, Bonney has been&nbsp;
the only character with a strong emotional story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:29.040
line for the entire egghead island arc. The&nbsp;
straw hats are basically just passing though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:37.020
and Vegapunk only got an introduction so far as&nbsp;
a character that needs a lift. Bonney is the only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:41.700
character that we actually see suffer here. While&nbsp;
we still don’t know much about her past, it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:47.640
clear from the little pieces that we have gotten,&nbsp;
that Bonney easily ticks the mark for tragic back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:54.360
story. She has had bad encounters with both of&nbsp;
Luffy’s arc nemesis, Blackbeard and Akainu and she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.360 --> 00:10:01.140
is even connected to Luffy’s father Dragon through&nbsp;
her own father Kuma. Kuma and in extension Bonney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:06.780
has been one of the most tragic and most intensely&nbsp;
developed characters throughout the entire story.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:11.880
We know that her dream is to take down the&nbsp;
world government and the celestial dragons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:17.820
for what they did to her and her father. And this&nbsp;
of course aligns perfectly with Luffy’s journey.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:22.200
It’s easy to see that bonney is in a&nbsp;
really dark place right now, and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:28.260
Luffy is probably gonna be the one to save her,&nbsp;
just like he did with the other straw hats. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:32.820
already saved Bonney physically from drowning,&nbsp;
but I think that Luffy will also be the one to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:37.860
save Bonney from her Darkness and pain, very&nbsp;
similar to how he did with Nami and Robin.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:43.140
And I think Bonney also would make a fantastic&nbsp;
addition to the crew. As we’ve seen over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:48.240
course of the story, she is basically a female&nbsp;
version of Luffy, cheerful, strong willed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:54.420
a strong sense of justice and of course a major&nbsp;
glutton. On top of that, she formed a real bond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.420 --> 00:11:00.000
with both Chopper and Jinbei extremely quickly&nbsp;
and she also kept Zoro from cutting down a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.660
celestial dragon back on Sabaody, though she was&nbsp;
clearly impressed by Luffy and Zoro being willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:12.060
to attack the world nobles. Similarly to Robin,&nbsp;
Bonney belongs with the straw hats, because they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:17.460
are the only ones willing to declare war on the&nbsp;
government that has chased them their entire life.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:21.840
As the daughter of a king, not only would&nbsp;
Bonney finally fill the empty princess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:26.700
slot in the straw hat crew, but as a member of&nbsp;
the worst generation, she would also be strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:33.300
enough to fight with the rest of the crew. That&nbsp;
plus her incredibly powerful devil fruit powers.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:38.640
It’s really hard to say who of these three women&nbsp;
will join Luffy. It could be that once again Oda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:44.280
denies us a new member as he’s done so often&nbsp;
before. Or it could also be that all 3 join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:50.700
at once. Who knows. Bonney and Stussy would&nbsp;
make perfect additions to the crew and Vivi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:56.100
as a quasi straw hat is about to reunite&nbsp;
with the crew thanks to Big News Morgans.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:12:01.620
And by the way, don’t you find it odd how&nbsp;
interested Morgan seems to be in Luffy. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:07.380
was even the case all the way back during whole&nbsp;
cake island. And Morgans also knows Stussy. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:12.240
mgiht not know that Morgans isn’t a mink or&nbsp;
an animal that can talk. Instead he is a man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:17.640
that has eaten the Albatros devil fruit and is&nbsp;
constantly in his hybrid form to disguise his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:22.620
true identity. Who could this man really be?&nbsp;
Well what if I told you that Big News Morgans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:28.380
might actually be a former member of the Roger&nbsp;
Pirates and maybe even Nami’s long lost father.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:33.480
If you want to find out more, you can watch that&nbsp;
entire theory right here. Shanks for watching.

